      "role": "user",
      "content": "The resource handle point is interesting—I'll dig into that. But the most frustrating part is the lack of pattern. It feels like the leak is almost sentient; it just waits for the system to be under a certain amount of load or for a specific sequence of interrupts to occur, and then it just... manifests. \n\nIt’s incredibly elusive. Is there a way to write a watchdog or a diagnostic tool that can \"trap\" these kinds of intermittent, almost ghost-like errors when they happen in real-time, without the overhead of a full debugger?",
